KJV renders: Shuhamites.

H7750.strongs:
Origin: or (by permutation) סוּט; a primitive root;
Meaning: to detrude, i.e. (intransitively and figuratively) become derelict (wrongly practise; namely, idolatry)
KJV renders: turn aside to.

H7751.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to push forth; (but used only figuratively) to lash, i.e. (the sea with oars) to row; by implication, to travel
KJV renders: go (about, through, to and fro), mariner, rower, run to and fro.

H7752.strongs:
Origin: from 7751;
Meaning: a lash (literally or figuratively)
KJV renders: scourge, whip.

H7753.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to entwine, i.e. shut in (for formation, protection or restraint)
KJV renders: fence, (make an) hedge (up).

H7754.strongs:
Origin: or (feminine) שׂוֹכָה; from 7753;
Meaning: a branch (as interleaved)
KJV renders: bough.

H7755.strongs:
Origin: or שֹׂכֹה; or שׂוֹכוֹ; from 7753;
Meaning: Sokoh or Soko, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV renders: Shocho, Shochoh, Sochoh, Soco, Socoh.

H7756.strongs:
Origin: probably patronymic from a name corresponding to 7754 (feminine);
Meaning: a Sukathite or descendant of an unknown Israelite named Sukah
KJV renders: Suchathite.

H7757.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to hang down;
Meaning: a skirt; by implication, a bottom edge
KJV renders: hem, skirt, train.

H7758.strongs:
Origin: or שֵׁילָל; (Micah 1:8), from 7997;
Meaning: nude (especially bare-foot); by implication, captive
KJV renders: spoiled, stripped.

H7759.strongs:
Origin: from 7999;
Meaning: peaceful (with the article always prefixed, making it a pet name); the Shulammith, an epithet of Solomon's queen
KJV renders: Shulamite.

H7760.strongs:
Origin: or שִׂים; a primitive root;
Meaning: to put (used in a great variety of applications, literal, figurative, inferentially, and elliptically)
KJV renders: × any wise, appoint, bring, call (a name), care, cast in, change, charge, commit, consider, convey, determine, disguise, dispose, do, get, give, heap up, hold, impute, lay (down, up), leave, look, make (out), mark, name, × on, ordain, order, paint, place, preserve, purpose, put (on), regard, rehearse, reward, (cause to) set (on, up), shew, stedfastly, take, × tell, tread down, (over-)turn, × wholly, work.

H7762.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to exhale;
Meaning: garlic (from its rank odor)
KJV renders: garlic.

H7763.strongs:
Origin: or שֹׁמֵר; active participle of 8104; keeper;
Meaning: Shomer, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Shomer.

H7764.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to rest; quiet;
Meaning: Shuni, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shuni.

H7765.strongs:
Origin: patronymic from 7764;
Meaning: a Shunite (collectively) or descendants of Shuni
KJV renders: Shunites.

H7766.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 7764; quietly;
Meaning: Shunem, a place in Pal
KJV renders: Shunem.

H7767.strongs:
Origin: patrial from 7766;
Meaning: a Shunammitess, or female inhabitant of Shunem
KJV renders: Shunamite.

H7768.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to be free; but used only causatively and reflexively, to halloo (for help, i.e. freedom from some trouble)
KJV renders: cry (aloud, out), shout.

H7769.strongs:
Origin: from 7768;
Meaning: a halloo
KJV renders: cry, riches.

H7770.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7769;
Meaning: Shua, a Canaanite
KJV renders: Shua, Shuah.

H7771.strongs:
Origin: from 7768 in the original sense of freedom;
Meaning: a noble, i.e. liberal, opulent; also (as noun in the derived sense) a halloo
KJV renders: bountiful, crying, rich.

H7772.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7771; rich;
Meaning: Shoa, an Oriental people
KJV renders: Shoa.

H7773.strongs:
Origin: from 7768;
Meaning: a halloo
KJV renders: cry.

H7774.strongs:
Origin: from 7768; wealth;
Meaning: Shua, an Israelitess
KJV renders: Shua.

H7775.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 7773;
Meaning: a hallooing
KJV renders: crying.

H7776.strongs:
Origin: or שֻׁעָל; from the same as 8168;
Meaning: a jackal (as a burrower)
KJV renders: fox.

H7777.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7776;
Meaning: Shual, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Shual.

H7778.strongs:
Origin: or שֹׁעֵר active participle of 8176 (as denominative from 8179);
Meaning: a janitor
KJV renders: doorkeeper, porter.

H7779.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to gape, i.e. snap at; figuratively, to overwhelm
KJV renders: break, bruise, cover.

H7780.strongs:
Origin: from 8210; poured;
Meaning: Shophak, a Syrian
KJV renders: Shophach.

H7781.strongs:
Origin: patronymic from 8197;
Meaning: a Shuphamite (collectively) or descendants of Shephupham
KJV renders: Shuphamite.

H7782.strongs:
Origin: or שֹׁפָר; from 8231 in the original sense of incising;
Meaning: a cornet (as giving a clear sound) or curved horn
KJV renders: cornet, trumpet.

H7783.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to run after or over, i.e. overflow
KJV renders: overflow, water.

H7784.strongs:
Origin: from 7783;
Meaning: a street (as run over)
KJV renders: street.

H7785.strongs:
Origin: from 7783;
Meaning: the (lower) leg (as a runner)
KJV renders: hip, leg, shoulder, thigh.

H7786.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to vanquish; by implication, to rule (causatively, crown)
KJV renders: make princes, have power, reign. See 5493.

H7787.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (identical with 7786 through the idea of reducing to pieces; compare 4883);
Meaning: to saw
KJV renders: cut.

H7788.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to turn, i.e. travel about (as a harlot or a merchant)
KJV renders: go, singular See also 7891.

H7789.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of going round for inspection);
Meaning: to spy out, i.e. (generally) survey, (for evil) lurk for, (for good) care for
KJV renders: behold, lay wait, look, observe, perceive, regard, see.

H7790.strongs:
Origin: from 7889;
Meaning: a foe (as lying in wait)
KJV renders: enemy.

H7791.strongs:
Origin: from 7788;
Meaning: a wall (as going about)
KJV renders: wall.

H7793.strongs:
Origin: the same as 7791;
Meaning: Shur, a region of the Desert
KJV renders: Shur.

H7794.strongs:
Origin: from 7788;
Meaning: a bullock (as a traveller)
KJV renders: bull(-ock), cow, ox, wall (by mistake for 7791).

H7795.strongs:
Origin: from 7786 in the primitive sense of 5493;
Meaning: properly, a ring, i.e. (by analogy) a row (adverbially)
KJV renders: principal.

H7796.strongs:
Origin: the same as 8321; a vine;
Meaning: Sorek, a valley in Palestine
KJV renders: Sorek.

H7797.strongs:
Origin: or שִׂישׂ; a primitive root;
Meaning: to be bright, i.e. cheerful
KJV renders: be glad, × greatly, joy, make mirth, rejoice.

H7798.strongs:
Origin: from 7797; joyful;
Meaning: Shavsha, an Israelite
KJV renders: Shavsha.

H7799.strongs:
Origin: or שׁוֹשָׁן; or שֹׁשָׁן; and (feminine) שׁוֹשַׁנָּה; from 7797;
Meaning: a lily (from its whiteness), as a flower of architectural ornament; also a (straight) trumpet (from the tubular shape)
KJV renders: lily, Shoshannim.
